WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.167
You've been on our show
many times.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.968
You've cooked for us.
We've done games.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.834
Do you remember the one
where I was upside down?

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:11.200
-I still remember.
-Yeah, it's like I thought maybe

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.000
you could taste food differently
if you were upside down,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.801
and it tastes the same, yeah.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.968
I want to talk about this
because, obviously, a lot of

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.901
people are fans of you
and Eleven Madison Park,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.334
and all these restaurants had
closed at the start

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:28.267
of the pandemic, and then you
reopened last summer.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:32.033
And you just announced that
it's all plant-based.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.868
You changed the --
I mean, you won awards.

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.567
You were the best restaurant
in the world.

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:38.901
Why would you take that risk
and what happened?

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:42.634
-You know, when I started
the career, I went at it

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:46.434
with an athlete's mentality, and
I wanted to work for the best.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.167
I wanted to be the best.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:52.601
I wanted to reach every accolade
that was out there.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:55.601
And as you said, in 2017,

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.801
we became the best restaurant
in the world.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:04.501
And shortly thereafter,
the pandemic hit,

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:07.968
and it was devastating
for our industry.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:14.267
And it gave us time to sit back
and rethink everything.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:19.133
And I was thinking about that
mountain top that I climbed

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:26.033
for so many years and how broken
so many of those systems were

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:30.167
and also how empty I felt

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:35.868
and that there is much more
to do than accolades.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:39.133
During the pandemic, not knowing
if there was going to be

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.634
a future of Eleven Madison Park,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.501
I turned the restaurant
into a community kitchen,

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:47.534
and we cooked over
a million meals

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.400
for food-insecure New Yorkers.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.901
-Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:55.701
That's awesome. Amazing, buddy.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:02:00.701
-And as good as that was,
of course,

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.167
it really filled my tank.

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:07.400
It was really satisfying, and I
reconnected with food in a way

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.834
I wasn't connected to
in a very long time.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.033
And I realized that food
can make change

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.300
and that food is my language.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.734
So when it was time to reopen
the restaurant, for me,

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:22.934
it was crystal clear that
the future was plant-based

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:26.467
and that the world didn't need
another preparation of

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:29.801
butter-poached lobster
or crispy skinned duck.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:33.501
We needed to use our creativity
to make that future

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:36.300
more delicious, more beautiful,
more meaningful.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.534
-So, you created
Eleven Madison Home --

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.267
I want to show everyone.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.834
This is the box.
This is the box you get.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.634
And right now it's
in New York City, right?

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.234
But if you go to
elevenmadisonhome.com,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.901
you sign up for this, and then
what is your mission with this?

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:55.868
-You know, so many of our guests
now leaving the restaurant are

00:02:55.868 --> 00:03:00.434
telling me, "Oh, if plant-based
could be like this,

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:03.133
I would eat plant-based
all the time."

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:07.467
And so the idea of this is --
and it's not a new idea --

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:12.701
but it is much more urgent
than it has been.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:16.400
And so the mission is to eat
plant-based one day a week.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.801
We can all make a change,
one day a week,

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:23.200
and it will make a huge change
on the planet.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.934
-You were nice enough to give me
one of the first boxes.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:30.300
Early on, I had COVID
and I didn't leave my house,

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.601
like you're supposed to do.
I was by myself.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:36.267
I said, "hey, bud, if you have
any spare food, I'm here.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.734
I'm by myself."

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:39.400
And you go, "well, I'm actually
doing this thing."

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.067
And you sent me this box and
it's the most beautiful thing.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.701
I just want to show you what you
get when you get the box.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:47.501
You open the box, and it is just
like this.

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.067
We didn't just do this for TV.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.567
It looks -- This is beautiful.

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:53.300
Like that. And this is
a full day --

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.834
breakfast, lunch,
dinner, snacks --

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:59.901
of the most amazing food and
a nice, beautifully written --

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:02.968
You have a story about the food,
where it comes from, the farms,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.634
how you can make it
if there are things to make.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.667
Sometimes they're just stuff
you eat out of the jar.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.400
-It's meant to be
really super simple.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.868
It's meant to tell a story as
well, like the restaurant does.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:17.400
-It's the freshest carrots.
-Oats and carrots.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.734
We also have products in here
of other people that we love

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:25.234
who are doing great things
in the plant space.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:28.367
-And when you buy this, also,
you give back as well, right?

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.667
-So, for us, it was clear that
after the pandemic,

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:35.434
I wanted to create
this circular ecosystem

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.267
at Eleven Madison Park.

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:43.367
Every diner makes five meals
for people

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:44.901
in need with every reservation.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:48.667
And so it was clear that with
every business going forward,

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.100
that has to be built
into the business.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.000
And so it is with this box
as well.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.767
-Yeah, so you're giving back
as well.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:58.868
I can't even tell you what
a risk, what a gamble this is,

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:01.133
but what a great thing
you're doing,

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.467
and you deserve all the props
in the world.

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.467
You're brilliant.
You're a genius.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:06.767
-Not really, but appreciate it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.501
-I love having you on.

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.701
Daniel Humm. Chef Daniel Humm.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.901
To sign up for
Eleven Madison Home,

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.801
go to elevenmadisonhome.com.

